# Dependencies.
# BOTH forms, deliberately: `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, so a node_modules SYMLINK — which is
# what a git worktree sharing an install has — is not ignored and gets committed by `git add -A`. That
# happened (2026-08-17): the symlinks landed in a commit, and pulling it REPLACED a real node_modules with
# a link to itself, deleting the install.
node_modules
node_modules/

# Subagent-driven-development workspace: ledgers, task briefs, reports, review
# packages. Scratch for a single run — the git history is the durable record now.
.superpowers/

# Persisted capability approvals (R-27).
#
# This is NOT ordinary noise-filtering. `.pi/grants-approvals.json` records that a
# human approved a gated capability — `tool:write@docs-writer` and the like. Committing
# it would mean one person's "always allow" silently authorising everyone who clones the
# repo, none of whom was asked. The loader already refuses entries whose `cwd` does not
# match (that is the real defence), but the file has no business in history either.
.pi/grants-approvals.json

# Grant ledgers: append-only audit trails, machine-local by nature.
.pi/grants.jsonl
*.jsonl.log

# Build output — reproduced by `npm run build`, and the source of truth is src/.
dist/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Logs and scratch
*.log
tmp/

.claude/
